funny-smelling thirty-pound sweaters with small arthropods living in them had driven them all into honest poverty and then not-so-honest poverty and led to their forcible transportation to Australia.","ref":"1999, Neal Stephenson, Cryptonomicon:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,65]],"id":"306a425c-22e3-4aaf-a7df-3e3e7c14ffd9"}],"categories":["English adjectives","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English terms derived from Latin","English terms with archaic senses","English terms with quotations","English undefined derivations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations"],"links":[["Unspeakable","unspeakable"],["appalling","appalling"]],"raw_glosses":["(archaic) Unspeakable, appalling."],"glosses":["Unspeakable, appalling."],"tags":["archaic"],"id":"eb09a660-0063-4ca1-90dc-0c493f975a5f"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Nefertiti":{"id":"f8592752-5321-4965-909d-58e9defbc06f","word":"Nefertiti","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"a queen of Ancient Egypt","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Nefertiti"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["queen","queen"],["consort","consort"],["pharaoh","pharaoh"],["Akhenaten","Akhenaten"]],"glosses":["A queen of Ancient Egypt, the chief consort of the pharaoh Akhenaten."],"id":"e13ab5c9-7193-4668-a9f6-7354c92dd4db"},{"categories":["English female given names","English female given names from Egyptian","English given names","English terms with rare senses"],"links":[["given name","given name"]],"raw_glosses":["(rare) A female given name from Egyptian."],"glosses":["A female given name from Egyptian."],"tags":["rare"],"id":"e4afe3f7-e796-44c0-8c09-5832f7371582"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]}}
